# Store-release and listing scripts are kept local only.
/scripts/

# Credentials and signing material.
#
# Nothing matching these is in the repository, and the release tooling reads
# every secret from ~/Development/secret at run time (see scripts/README.md),
# so these are a backstop rather than a description of what is here: a key or
# a profile dropped into the tree by Xcode, fastlane, or a hurried hand should
# never become a commit.
*.p8
*.p12
*.pfx
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
*.keystore
*.jks
.env
.env.*
*.env
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# Xcode export configuration. Carries the team id and the names of the
# provisioning profiles a build is signed with; the macOS one this project
# actually uses lives in the ignored /scripts/ directory.
ExportOptions.plist

# Build output that is signed, or that embeds absolute paths from this
# machine. /build/ already covers the usual location — these catch the copies
# that get left beside the project.
*.xcarchive/
*.dSYM/
*.ipa
*.pkg
*.aab
*.apk